    - target: {fileID: 8021706265186088782, guid: a21a9ca0325425f42ae2532455c4dfb6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_LocalEulerAnglesHint.y
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8021706265186088782, guid: a21a9ca0325425f42ae2532455c4dfb6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_LocalEulerAnglesHint.z
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8099463261135127859, guid: a21a9ca0325425f42ae2532455c4dfb6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'Officials have noticed an unusual pattern during the current season:
        several records that appeared unbeatable only months ago have suddenly been
        surpassed.

        At first, the extraordinary performances were celebrated
        as evidence that athletes were reaching new levels of ability. However, as
        one record after another disappeared, questions began to emerge.

        Some
        experts argue that improved training explains the sudden progress. Others
        believe that the sport may be experiencing an unprecedented technological
        revolution.

        The Racing Committee has taken a more cautious position.
        Every new record will now be examined carefully before being added to the
        official books.

        For athletes, this means that crossing the finish
        line first may no longer be enough. Their time must also survive the scrutiny
        of officials, inspectors, and increasingly suspicious spectators.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8099463261135127859, guid: a21a9ca0325425f42ae2532455c4dfb6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_margin.w
